'''''Brunfelsia uniflora''''' (syn. ''Brunfelsia hopeana''), the '''manac''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Solanaceae]].<ref name="RHS_2432" >{{cite web |title=''Brunfelsia uniflora'' manac |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/2432/i-brunfelsia-uniflora-i/details |date=2022 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=8 November 2022 |quote=Other common names; vegetable mercury }}</ref> It is native to [[Monos]] island of Trinidad and Tobago, Venezuela, the [[Venezuelan Antilles]], Guyana, Brazil, and northwest Argentina, and has been introduced to eastern Tropical Africa, [[Réunion]], [[Mauritius]], India, and [[Assam]].<ref name="POWO_814696-1" >{{cite POWO |id=814696-1 |title=''Brunfelsia uniflora'' (Pohl) D.Don |access-date=8 November 2022 }}</ref> A poisonous evergreen shrub typically {{cvt|0.5|to|3|m|ft|0}} tall, it is commonly cultivated as an ornamental, and as an ingredient in [[ayahuasca]] and other potions, usually under its synonym ''Brunfelsia hopeana''.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://greeninstitute.ng/plants/2019/2/11/brunfelsia-uniflora |title=''Brunfelsia uniflora'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=11 February 2019 |website=greeninstitute.ng |publisher=The Green Institute |access-date=8 November 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite book |title=The Healing Power of Rainforest Herbs: A Guide to Understanding and Using Herbal Medicinals |last1=Taylor |first1=Leslie |date=4 November 2005 |isbn=978-0757001444 |quote=Manacá }}</ref>

